   1+ 10C6              ; PROJECT126 / X86_MODRM v0.1.0
   2+ 10C6              ; Intel 8086 16-bit ModR/M effective-address decoder.
   3+ 10C6              ; Reference: PCem/808x.c fetcheal(), mod1add[] and mod1seg[].
   4+ 10C6              ;
   5+ 10C6              ; API:
   6+ 10C6              ;   x86_decode_modrm16 fetches the ModR/M byte from guest CS:IP.
   7+ 10C6              ;   OUT: x86_modrm_mod/reg/rm, x86_ea_is_reg, x86_ea_reg,
   8+ 10C6              ;        x86_ea_offset, x86_ea_segment.
   9+ 10C6              ;   Carry set on instruction-stream or displacement memory fault.
  10+ 10C6              ;
  11+ 10C6              ; Register encoding: AX,CX,DX,BX,SP,BP,SI,DI.
  12+ 10C6              ; Memory addressing follows the original 8086 BX/BP/SI/DI combinations.
  13+ 10C6              ; Default segment is SS for BP-based forms, DS otherwise.
  14+ 10C6              ; mod=00,r/m=110 is direct [disp16] and defaults to DS.
  15+ 10C6              ; Segment override prefixes are applied by the x86_exec prefix layer.
  16+ 10C6              ; All guest instruction bytes are fetched via x86_cpu_fetch8/fetch16.
  17+ 10C6
  18+ 10C6              x86_decode_modrm16:
